## MEETING MINUTES

### Update Data standardisation exercises

#### 1) ICEG Person

- The ICEG Person trajectory was restarted in May 2026 with all federal and regional partners.
- During the Business Workshop on 24/06/2026, eight use cases were presented by different partners.
- Based on the workshop results, the scope was confirmed as the development of an ICEG Person model serving as a national reference model across all levels of government, using the National Register information types as the starting point.
- Four thematic workshops have been planned:
  - Core Identification (21/09/2026)
  - Address & Residence (19/10/2026)
  - Family & Civil Status (19/11/2026)
  - Status, Documents & Special Cases (10/12/2026)
- Documentation, including charter, scope and meeting minutes, is available via GitHub.
- During the workshops, concepts, attributes, cardinalities, datatypes and relations will be discussed.
- Deliverables will be published through BELGIF.

**Timeline**
- Consolidation of the model is planned after completion of the fourth thematic workshop.
- Publication of version 1 is foreseen by the end of 2026 or in Q1 2027.

**Action**
- The workshop invitations and documentation links will be circulated to the members of the Review Committee.
- Members are encouraged to forward the invitations to relevant colleagues and stakeholders within their organisations.

#### 2) ICEG Hydrants

- An update was provided on the ICEG Hydrants exercise.
- The feedback gathered during the previous working group cycle has been processed.
- In total, 43 change requests were analysed and handled.
- A draft publication is now available on BELGIF.
- Some minor technical publication issues remain and are currently being resolved.

**Next steps**
- Organise a stakeholder workshop in October 2026.
- Organise a closing webinar in November 2026.
- Finalise the model based on the feedback received.

